========================================================================================================================
                                       TROUBLESHOOTING COMMON NETWORK STATES
========================================================================================================================

STATE / ISSUE                 | CAUSE / SYMPTOM                      | RESOLUTION COMMANDS
------------------------------+--------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------
Network is inactive           | The network has stopped or was       | 1. Check state: virsh net-info default

                              | never started. VMs cannot connect.   | 2. Start it:    virsh net-start default
------------------------------+--------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------
Autostart is disabled         | Network stays down after a host      | 1. Enable it:   virsh net-autostart default

                              | system reboot.                       | 2. Verify:      virsh net-list --all
------------------------------+--------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------
Bridge interface missing      | The virtual bridge (e.g. virbr0) did | 1. Restart libvirtd service: 

                              | not get created in the system kernel |    systemctl restart libvirtd
                              | when the network started.            | 2. Re-trigger net: virsh net-destroy default &&
                              |                                      |                    virsh net-start default
------------------------------+--------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------
IP Address Conflict           | The IP range defined in the XML      | 1. Dump XML:    virsh net-dumpxml default

                              | overlaps with an existing host route | 2. Check route: ip route show
                              | or physical network.                 | 3. Fix range:   virsh net-edit default
------------------------------+--------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------
DHCP Not Assigning IPs        | The dnsmasq process managed by       | 1. Kill stray dnsmasq: killall dnsmasq

                              | libvirt is hung or conflicting with  | 2. Restart net: virsh net-destroy default &&
                              | a system-wide dnsmasq instance.      |                 virsh net-start default
========================================================================================================================
